                <pb facs="0675" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg595"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic">May 19,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Powell inquires if he may take the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Topeka</hi> to St. Marc to consult with the commander of the army of the
                    north and advise him not to go to Port au Prince. He states that if the army,
                    which is said to number 5,000 men, is not prevented from reaching Port au
                    Prince, a severe contest is to be expected, in which American interests will
                    suffer.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
